        "title": "China sends first foreign astronaut to ISS rival as it globalises space operations",
        "source": "The Guardian - Science",
        "source_id": "guardian_science",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/25/china-sends-first-pakistani-astronaut-into-space",
        "published_at": "2026-11-25T14:18:29",
        "level": "C1",
        "slot_level": "C1",
        "source_level": "C1",
        "word_count": 663,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "China has flown the first foreign astronaut to its Tiangong space station, starting what it says will be the globalisation of its space operations as the US-led International Space Station (ISS) enters its final years of operation.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "5e1f527f643bdda33d09fa1f919ed2b2b440d88c",
        "summary": "Muhammad Zeeshan Ali – the first Pakistani to reach orbit – greeted with Chinese ‘space handshake’ at Tiangong station China has flown the first foreign astronaut to its Tiangong space station, starting what it says will be the globalisation of its space operations as the US-led International Space Station (ISS) enters its final years of operation. Floating through a hatch to enter Tiangong, Pakistan’s Muhammad Zeeshan Ali grinned broadly as he was embraced by the onboard crew in what China’s space agency called the country’s first foreign “space handshake”.",
